
  <sn><md>### Organometallic Compounds

**Organometallic compounds** are chemical compounds that contain a **direct chemical bond between a carbon atom of an organic group and a metal atom**.

The general representation is:

$$
\mathrm{R-M}
$$

Where:

* $\mathrm{R}$ = organic group containing carbon
* $\mathrm{M}$ = metal

**Basic structure**

```text
Organic group
     |
     C — Metal
     |
   R-group
```

The key feature is the **direct C–metal bond**.

Examples

| Compound                | Formula                 | Metal     |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | --------- |
| Methyl lithium          | $\mathrm{CH_3Li}$       | Lithium   |
| Ethyl magnesium bromide | $\mathrm{C_2H_5MgBr}$   | Magnesium |
| Dimethylmercury         | $\mathrm{(CH_3)_2Hg}$   | Mercury   |
| Tetraethyllead          | $\mathrm{(C_2H_5)_4Pb}$ | Lead      |
| Ferrocene               | $\mathrm{Fe(C_5H_5)_2}$ | Iron      |
</md></sn>
